<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 2 April <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Baldwin I of Jerusalem</span><span class="tp">c. 1060–1118</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ruy-gonzalez-de-clavijo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ruy-gonzalez-de-clavijo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ruy González de Clavijo</span><span class="tp">d. 1412</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand I of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1380–1416</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand III, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1608–1657</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-luis-de-san-vitores"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-luis-de-san-vitores.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Diego Luis de San Vitores</span><span class="tp">1627–1672</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joseph-dudley"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joseph-dudley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joseph Dudley</span><span class="tp">1647–1720</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-gage"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-gage.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Gage</span><span class="tp">c. 1719–1787</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ranjitsinhji"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ranjitsinhji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ranjitsinhji</span><span class="tp">1872–1933</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
